      "content": "I get the need for a balanced draft, but my director isn't looking for a 'maybe'—they want a data-backed recommendation on which one actually works better for social stability. If you had to look at the data on wealth inequality and social unrest, which one of these isn't just a temporary fix, but a more robust solution for long-term stability? Like, if we want to actually stop the instability, which path is the more logical choice?",
